/-! # The eight-boundary-point gate, Lemma 1 – Theorem 12 (`hand/EIGHT_BOUNDARY.md`)

**Role.** Primary route. `UNRESTRICTED.md` §4 (lines 126–130) cites Theorem 13
(`Heilbronn/Eight/EightBoundary.lean`) for every configuration with at least eight boundary
points; Theorem 13 is also used by `SIX_BOUNDARY_TWO_SIDE_PROJECTION` §4. Lemma 3 and the §4 scalar
bound (`claim_scalar_bound`) are reused by `SEVEN_BOUNDARY_TOP_CAP` and
`SEVEN_BOUNDARY_TOP_CAP_RIGHT`. This file holds the results that Theorem 13 assembles.

**Setting.** The normal form of `Heilbronn/Eight/EightBoundary/Setting.lean` (`EightAnchors`,
`O ∈ (0,1)²`, `octagon`, `eightConfig`). In the manuscript `s` is twice the minimum area, a
variable; the side gaps are `L = h-a`, `B = c-b`, `R = e-d`, `T = f-g`. Regions are written with
`InPolygon` (open) and `InClosedPolygon` (closed) of `Heilbronn/Eight/RadialCatalogue.lean`,
listing the vertices counterclockwise, e.g. `△ADE = ![(0,a), (1,d), (1,e)]`; the corner caps are
`conv(B,C,D,E)` and `conv(D,E,F,G)`; the central region (11) is `InCentralRegion (octagon …)`.

**Results.**
* `lemma1`: nine distinct points, no three collinear, at least eight on the boundary: exactly
  eight, no corner, two on each open side, the ninth in the open square;
* `claim_normal_form`: consequently a configuration of positive minimum area with eight boundary
  points is a relabelling of `eightConfig` in normal form;
* `claim_thresholds`: the rational comparisons `(5-2√6)/2 < 3/58 < 17/320 < A₀`, `7/128 < A₀`,
  `21/400 < 17/320`, `(3-2√2)/4 < 1/20 < 17/320`;
* `theorem2`: `O` outside the open octagon gives minimum area `≤ (5-2√6)/2`;
* `lemma3`: the five-point quadrilateral inequality `Q ≥ 2(1+√2)s`;
* `claim_scalar_bound`: the scalar contradiction (6)–(10) of §4;
* `theorem4`: `O` in a closed side quadrilateral gives minimum area `< 7/128`;
* `corollary5`: at minimum area `≥ A₀`, `O` is in the central region (11);
* `theorem6`: `O ∈ ADE ∩ HDE ∩ BCF ∩ BCG` gives `≤ (5-2√6)/2`;
* `lemma7`: `s ≤ m(1-m)/2`, `m` the largest side gap;
* `theorem8`: central region and both corner caps give `≤ 21/400`;
* `theorem9`: `O ∈ ADE ∩ HDE ∩ BFG ∩ BCG` gives `< 1/20`;
* `lemma10`: disjoint opposite contact intervals give `≤ (3-2√2)/4`;
* `theorem11`: central region, `ADE ∩ HDE`, cap `BCDE`, not cap `DEFG` give `< 7/128`;
* `theorem12`: central region, `ADE ∩ HDE`, `BCF ∩ CFG`, outside both caps give `< 7/128`.

Implicit in the manuscript: "the eight boundary points have the form in Lemma 1" is
`EightAnchors a b c d e f g h` and `InOpenSquare O`. Theorems 6 and 9 add "the conclusion also holds
for every square-symmetry image of these conditions"; that clause is the stated theorem composed
with `SquareSymmetry.minTriangleArea_comp`, `minTriangleArea_comp_perm` and
`RadialCatalogue.claim_symmetry_relabel`, and is not stated separately. Lemmas 7 and 10 use only
boundary triangles and are stated for the eight boundary points (`octagon`), which implies the
nine-point form.

Stale text (not formalized): lines 3–7 say the note "does not yet remove all orientation
assumptions"; Theorem 13 and lines 1041–1046 supersede this.

**Proofs.** The scalar chains are in `Heilbronn/Eight/EightBoundary/Scalar.lean` (real-variable
cores, divisions `s/L` replaced by auxiliary variables), the boundary budgets, Lemma 3 and the
`ABCD` case of Theorem 4 in `Support.lean`, the counting of Lemma 1 in `Incidence.lean`. The
symmetry reductions of Theorems 2 and 4 ("by a square symmetry") use
`RadialCatalogue.transfer`. Theorems 11 and 12 are proved by polynomial certificates
(`Cert11.lean`, `Cert12.lean`, data in `data/eight/`, generated by `scripts/eight/certs.py`)
instead of the long scalar arguments of §§9–10: at doubled area `7/64`, the eleven (resp.
fourteen) oriented `O`-triangles forced by the hypotheses, the budgets, the gap bounds `≤ 11/16`
(Lemma 7) and the overlaps of Lemma 10 are incompatible (`base_of_min` collects these facts).
Theorem 8 does not need the ear argument of lines 486–490: `d ≤ y ≤ e` follows directly from the
two cap edges `EB`, `GD`.
-/

@[expose] public section

noncomputable section
namespace Heilbronn.EightBoundary

open RadialCatalogue

/-! ### §1. Boundary incidences -/

/-- **Lemma 1** (`EIGHT_BOUNDARY:Lemma1`). Nine distinct points of the unit square, no three
collinear, at least eight on its boundary: exactly eight are on the boundary, none is a corner,
each open side contains exactly two of them, and the ninth point is in the open square.
`hand/EIGHT_BOUNDARY.md`, lines 11–27.
Uses: standard fact (a side holding three points makes them collinear). -/
theorem lemma1 (P : Fin 9 → Point) (hP : ∀ i, P i ∈ unitSquare) (hinj : Function.Injective P)
    (hncol : ∀ i j k, i ≠ j → j ≠ k → i ≠ k → sarea (P i) (P j) (P k) ≠ 0)
    (h8 : 8 ≤ {i : Fin 9 | OnSquareBoundary (P i)}.ncard) :
    {i : Fin 9 | OnSquareBoundary (P i)}.ncard = 8 ∧ (∀ i, ¬ IsCorner (P i)) ∧
      {i : Fin 9 | OnLeftSide (P i)}.ncard = 2 ∧ {i : Fin 9 | OnBottomSide (P i)}.ncard = 2 ∧
      {i : Fin 9 | OnRightSide (P i)}.ncard = 2 ∧ {i : Fin 9 | OnTopSide (P i)}.ncard = 2 ∧
      ∀ i, ¬ OnSquareBoundary (P i) → InOpenSquare (P i) := by
  classical
  simp only [ncard_eq_card_filter] at h8 ⊢
  obtain ⟨hbd, hcor, hL, hB, hR, hT⟩ := lemma1_core P hP hncol h8
  have open1 : ∀ i, (P i).1 = 0 ∨ (P i).1 = 1 → 0 < (P i).2 ∧ (P i).2 < 1 := by
    intro i hi
    obtain ⟨_, _, h3, h4⟩ := hP i
    exact ⟨lt_of_le_of_ne h3 fun h => hcor i ⟨hi, Or.inl h.symm⟩,
      lt_of_le_of_ne h4 fun h => hcor i ⟨hi, Or.inr h⟩⟩
  have open2 : ∀ i, (P i).2 = 0 ∨ (P i).2 = 1 → 0 < (P i).1 ∧ (P i).1 < 1 := by
    intro i hi
    obtain ⟨h1, h2, _, _⟩ := hP i
    exact ⟨lt_of_le_of_ne h1 fun h => hcor i ⟨Or.inl h.symm, hi⟩,
      lt_of_le_of_ne h2 fun h => hcor i ⟨Or.inr h, hi⟩⟩
  have eqL : (Finset.univ.filter fun i => OnLeftSide (P i)) =
      Finset.univ.filter fun i => (P i).1 = 0 :=
    Finset.filter_congr fun i _ => ⟨fun h => h.1, fun h => ⟨h, open1 i (Or.inl h)⟩⟩
  have eqR : (Finset.univ.filter fun i => OnRightSide (P i)) =
      Finset.univ.filter fun i => (P i).1 = 1 :=
    Finset.filter_congr fun i _ => ⟨fun h => h.1, fun h => ⟨h, open1 i (Or.inr h)⟩⟩
  have eqB : (Finset.univ.filter fun i => OnBottomSide (P i)) =
      Finset.univ.filter fun i => (P i).2 = 0 :=
    Finset.filter_congr fun i _ => ⟨fun h => h.1, fun h => ⟨h, open2 i (Or.inl h)⟩⟩
  have eqT : (Finset.univ.filter fun i => OnTopSide (P i)) =
      Finset.univ.filter fun i => (P i).2 = 1 :=
    Finset.filter_congr fun i _ => ⟨fun h => h.1, fun h => ⟨h, open2 i (Or.inr h)⟩⟩
  refine ⟨hbd, hcor, by rw [eqL]; exact hL, by rw [eqB]; exact hB, by rw [eqR]; exact hR,
    by rw [eqT]; exact hT, fun i hi => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨h1, h2, h3, h4⟩ := hP i
  simp only [OnSquareBoundary, not_and, not_or] at hi
  obtain ⟨n1, n2, n3, n4⟩ := hi (hP i)
  exact ⟨lt_of_le_of_ne h1 (Ne.symm n1), lt_of_le_of_ne h2 n2, lt_of_le_of_ne h3 (Ne.symm n3),
    lt_of_le_of_ne h4 n4⟩

/-- **Claim** (`EIGHT_BOUNDARY:claim-normal-form`). A configuration of the square with positive
minimum area and at least eight boundary points is, after fixing the counterclockwise labels, a
relabelling of the normal form: `P ∘ σ = eightConfig a b c d e f g h O` with
`EightAnchors a b c d e f g h` and `O` in the open square.
`hand/EIGHT_BOUNDARY.md`, lines 29–50.
Uses: EIGHT_BOUNDARY:Lemma1. -/
theorem claim_normal_form (P : Fin 9 → Point) (hP : ∀ i, P i ∈ unitSquare)
    (hpos : 0 < minTriangleArea P) (h8 : 8 ≤ {i : Fin 9 | OnSquareBoundary (P i)}.ncard) :
    ∃ (a b c d e f g h : ℝ) (O : Point) (σ : Equiv.Perm (Fin 9)),
      EightAnchors a b c d e f g h ∧ InOpenSquare O ∧ P ∘ σ = eightConfig a b c d e f g h O := by
  classical
  rw [ncard_eq_card_filter] at h8
  exact normal_form_core P hP (fun i j k hij hjk hik => sarea_ne_zero_of_min_pos hpos i j k hij hjk hik) h8

/-- **Claim** (`EIGHT_BOUNDARY:claim-thresholds`, named here). The rational comparisons of the
note: `(5-2√6)/2 < 3/58 < 17/320 < A₀` (via `√6 > 71/29` and `p₀ < 7/40`, `A₀ = (2-9p₀)/8`),
`7/128 < A₀` (via `(145/18)² < 65`), `21/400 < 17/320` and `(3-2√2)/4 < 1/20 < 17/320`
(via `√2 > 7/5`).
`hand/EIGHT_BOUNDARY.md`, lines 134–142, 287–291, 531, 620–622, 659–660.
Uses: none. -/
theorem claim_thresholds :
    (5 - 2 * Real.sqrt 6) / 2 < 3 / 58 ∧ (3 : ℝ) / 58 < 17 / 320 ∧ (17 : ℝ) / 320 < A₀ ∧
      (7 : ℝ) / 128 < A₀ ∧ (21 : ℝ) / 400 < 17 / 320 ∧ (3 - 2 * Real.sqrt 2) / 4 < 1 / 20 ∧
      (1 : ℝ) / 20 < 17 / 320 := by
  have h6 := sqrt_six_bounds
  have h2 := sqrt_two_gt
  have hA := A₀_bounds
  refine ⟨by linarith, by norm_num, by linarith, hA.1, by norm_num, by linarith, by norm_num⟩

/-! ### §2. The ninth point is inside the octagon -/

/-- **Theorem 2** (`EIGHT_BOUNDARY:Theorem2`). In the normal form, if `O` is not in the open
boundary octagon (outside the convex hull of the eight boundary points, or on its boundary), the
minimum triangle area is at most `(5-2√6)/2 < A₀`.
`hand/EIGHT_BOUNDARY.md`, lines 54–142.
Uses: standard facts (`z + q/z ≥ 2√q`; `√(1+1/λ) + √(1+1/(1-λ)) ≥ 2√3`). -/
theorem theorem2 {a b c d e f g h : ℝ} {O : Point} (hA : EightAnchors a b c d e f g h)
    (hO : InOpenSquare O) (hout : ¬ InPolygon (octagon a b c d e f g h) O) :
    minTriangleArea (eightConfig a b c d e f g h O) ≤ (5 - 2 * Real.sqrt 6) / 2 := by
  simp only [InPolygon, not_forall, not_lt] at hout
  obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := hout
  have hcorner : ∀ r : Fin 4, sarea (octagon a b c d e f g h (Fin.ofNat 8 (2 * r.val)))
      (octagon a b c d e f g h (Fin.ofNat 8 (2 * r.val) + 1)) O ≤ 0 →
      minTriangleArea (eightConfig a b c d e f g h O) ≤ (5 - 2 * Real.sqrt 6) / 2 := by
    intro r hr
    obtain ⟨a', b', c', d', e', f', g', h', hA', hO', hoct, -, hmin⟩ := transfer false r hA hO
    rw [← hmin]
    refine theorem2_corner hA' hO' ?_
    rw [hoct 0, hoct 1, symOf_sarea]
    simpa [labelPerm, add_comm] using hr
  obtain ⟨x, y⟩ := O
  obtain ⟨hx0, hx1, hy0, hy1⟩ := hO
  obtain ⟨h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6, h7, h8, h9, h10, h11, h12⟩ := hA
  fin_cases i
  · exact hcorner 0 (by simpa using hi)
  · exfalso; simp [octagon, finRotate_apply, sarea] at hi; nlinarith
  · exact hcorner 1 (by simpa [finRotate_apply] using hi)
  · exfalso; simp [octagon, finRotate_apply, sarea] at hi; nlinarith
  · exact hcorner 2 (by simpa [finRotate_apply] using hi)
  · exfalso; simp [octagon, finRotate_apply, sarea] at hi; nlinarith
  · exact hcorner 3 (by simpa [finRotate_apply] using hi)
  · exfalso; simp [octagon, finRotate_apply, sarea] at hi; nlinarith

/-! ### §3. The five-point quadrilateral inequality -/

/-- **Lemma 3** (`EIGHT_BOUNDARY:Lemma3`). Let `V₁V₂V₃V₄` be a convex (counterclockwise)
quadrilateral and `O` a point of it. If every triangle on these five points has doubled area at
least `s > 0`, then the doubled area `Q = [V₁V₂V₃] + [V₁V₃V₄]` of the quadrilateral satisfies
`Q ≥ 2(1+√2)s`. (The manuscript takes `O` inside; a point on an edge gives a zero triangle,
which the hypothesis excludes.)
`hand/EIGHT_BOUNDARY.md`, lines 146–178.
Uses: standard facts (the identity `ac - bd = det(r₁,r₃)det(r₂,r₄)`; AM–GM). -/
theorem lemma3 {V₁ V₂ V₃ V₄ O : Point} {s : ℝ} (hs : 0 < s)
    (hconv : IsConvexPolygon ![V₁, V₂, V₃, V₄]) (hO : InClosedPolygon ![V₁, V₂, V₃, V₄] O)
    (hmin : s / 2 ≤ minTriangleArea ![V₁, V₂, V₃, V₄, O]) :
    2 * (1 + Real.sqrt 2) * s ≤ sarea V₁ V₂ V₃ + sarea V₁ V₃ V₄ :=
  lemma3_core hs hO hmin

/-! ### §4. The four side quadrilaterals -/

/-- **Claim** (`EIGHT_BOUNDARY:claim-scalar-bound`, named here). The scalar contradiction of §4,
(6)–(10), reused verbatim by `SEVEN_BOUNDARY_TOP_CAP` (3)–(4) and `SEVEN_BOUNDARY_TOP_CAP_RIGHT`
(11): if `s, X, Z > 0`, `sZ < 1`, `XZ ≥ 4`, and the quadrilateral bound (7)
`Q ≤ 2 - sZ - s(2-sZ)/(1-sZ) - X + 2s` is compatible with Lemma 3's `Q ≥ 2(1+√2)s`, then
`s < 7/64`. (Monotonicity in `z = sZ`, the substitution `u = 2s/X`, (8)–(9), `√2 > 7/5` and the
cubic `P(u) = 35 - 306u + 827u² - 640u³ > 0` on `(0, 1/2)`.)
`hand/EIGHT_BOUNDARY.md`, lines 231–286.
Uses: none. -/
theorem claim_scalar_bound {s X Z : ℝ} (hs : 0 < s) (hX : 0 < X) (hZ : 0 < Z) (hsZ : s * Z < 1)
    (hXZ : 4 ≤ X * Z)
    (hQ : 2 * (1 + Real.sqrt 2) * s ≤ 2 - s * Z - s * (2 - s * Z) / (1 - s * Z) - X + 2 * s) :
    s < 7 / 64 :=
  scalar_bound_core hs hX hsZ hXZ hQ

/-- **Theorem 4** (`EIGHT_BOUNDARY:Theorem4`). In the normal form, if `O` belongs to one of the
closed side quadrilaterals `conv(A,B,C,D)`, `conv(C,D,E,F)`, `conv(E,F,G,H)`, `conv(G,H,A,B)`, the
minimum triangle area is strictly less than `7/128 < A₀`.
`hand/EIGHT_BOUNDARY.md`, lines 182–294.
Uses: EIGHT_BOUNDARY:Lemma3, EIGHT_BOUNDARY:claim-scalar-bound. -/
theorem theorem4 {a b c d e f g h : ℝ} {O : Point} (hA : EightAnchors a b c d e f g h)
    (hO : InOpenSquare O)
    (hq : InClosedPolygon ![(0, a), (b, 0), (c, 0), (1, d)] O ∨
      InClosedPolygon ![(c, 0), (1, d), (1, e), (f, 1)] O ∨
      InClosedPolygon ![(1, e), (f, 1), (g, 1), (0, h)] O ∨
      InClosedPolygon ![(g, 1), (0, h), (0, a), (b, 0)] O) :
    minTriangleArea (eightConfig a b c d e f g h O) < 7 / 128 := by
  rcases hq with hq | hq | hq | hq
  · exact theorem4_ABCD hA hq
  · obtain ⟨a', b', c', d', e', f', g', h', hA', -, hoct, -, hmin⟩ := transfer false 1 hA hO
    rw [← hmin]
    exact theorem4_ABCD hA' (inClosedPolygon_rot 1 (fun i => by
      fin_cases i; exacts [hoct 0, hoct 1, hoct 2, hoct 3]) hq)
  · obtain ⟨a', b', c', d', e', f', g', h', hA', -, hoct, -, hmin⟩ := transfer false 2 hA hO
    rw [← hmin]
    exact theorem4_ABCD hA' (inClosedPolygon_rot 2 (fun i => by
      fin_cases i; exacts [hoct 0, hoct 1, hoct 2, hoct 3]) hq)
  · obtain ⟨a', b', c', d', e', f', g', h', hA', -, hoct, -, hmin⟩ := transfer false 3 hA hO
    rw [← hmin]
    exact theorem4_ABCD hA' (inClosedPolygon_rot 3 (fun i => by
      fin_cases i; exacts [hoct 0, hoct 1, hoct 2, hoct 3]) hq)

/-- **Corollary 5** (`EIGHT_BOUNDARY:Corollary5`). In the normal form with minimum triangle area
at least `A₀`, `O` is strictly inside the octagon, outside the four closed side quadrilaterals, and
in the central region (11) `int conv(A,D,E,H) ∩ int conv(B,C,F,G)`. (In particular it lies
outside all eight ears, and the first and fifth orientation expressions of `HAND_PROOF.md`
Theorem 1, `y - a - (d-a)x` and `c - x + (f-c)y`, are positive.)
`hand/EIGHT_BOUNDARY.md`, lines 296–317.
Uses: EIGHT_BOUNDARY:Theorem2, EIGHT_BOUNDARY:Theorem4, EIGHT_BOUNDARY:claim-thresholds. -/
theorem corollary5 {a b c d e f g h : ℝ} {O : Point} (hA : EightAnchors a b c d e f g h)
    (hO : InOpenSquare O) (hmin : A₀ ≤ minTriangleArea (eightConfig a b c d e f g h O)) :
    InPolygon (octagon a b c d e f g h) O ∧ OutsideSideQuads (octagon a b c d e f g h) O ∧
      InCentralRegion (octagon a b c d e f g h) O := by
  have hthr := claim_thresholds
  have hA0 := A₀_bounds
  have hin : InPolygon (octagon a b c d e f g h) O := by
    by_contra hout
    have := theorem2 hA hO hout
    linarith [hthr.1, hthr.2.1, hthr.2.2.1]
  have hq : OutsideSideQuads (octagon a b c d e f g h) O := by
    refine ⟨fun h => ?_, fun h => ?_, fun h => ?_, fun h => ?_⟩
    · have := theorem4 hA hO (Or.inl h); linarith
    · have := theorem4 hA hO (Or.inr (Or.inl h)); linarith
    · have := theorem4 hA hO (Or.inr (Or.inr (Or.inl h))); linarith
    · have := theorem4 hA hO (Or.inr (Or.inr (Or.inr h))); linarith
  refine ⟨hin, hq, ?_, ?_⟩
  · have q0 := pos_of_not_quad hin 0 (by simpa using hq.1)
    have q4 := pos_of_not_quad hin 4 (by simpa using hq.2.2.1)
    have i3 := hin 3
    have i7 := hin 7
    intro i
    fin_cases i
    · simp; rw [sarea_cycle]; simpa using q0
    · simpa [finRotate_apply] using i3
    · simp [finRotate_apply]; rw [sarea_cycle]; simpa using q4
    · simpa [finRotate_apply] using i7
  · have q2 := pos_of_not_quad hin 2 (by simpa using hq.2.1)
    have q6 := pos_of_not_quad hin 6 (by simpa using hq.2.2.2)
    have i1 := hin 1
    have i5 := hin 5
    intro i
    fin_cases i
    · simpa [finRotate_apply] using i1
    · simp [finRotate_apply]; rw [sarea_cycle]; simpa using q2
    · simpa [finRotate_apply] using i5
    · simp [finRotate_apply]; rw [sarea_cycle]; simpa using q6

/-! ### §5. Two adjacent double wedges -/

/-- **Theorem 6** (`EIGHT_BOUNDARY:Theorem6`). In the normal form, if `O` belongs to the closed
triangles `ADE`, `HDE`, `BCF` and `BCG`, the minimum triangle area is at most `(5-2√6)/2 < A₀`.
(The manuscript adds: also for every square-symmetry image of these conditions; see the module
docstring.)
`hand/EIGHT_BOUNDARY.md`, lines 325–446.
Uses: standard facts (AM–GM; `(5-2√6)(2+t) - t(1-t) = (t-(√6-2))²`). -/
theorem theorem6 {a b c d e f g h : ℝ} {O : Point} (hA : EightAnchors a b c d e f g h)
    (hO : InOpenSquare O)
    (hADE : InClosedPolygon ![(0, a), (1, d), (1, e)] O)
    (hHDE : InClosedPolygon ![(0, h), (1, d), (1, e)] O)
    (hBCF : InClosedPolygon ![(b, 0), (c, 0), (f, 1)] O)
    (hBCG : InClosedPolygon ![(b, 0), (c, 0), (g, 1)] O) :
    minTriangleArea (eightConfig a b c d e f g h O) ≤ (5 - 2 * Real.sqrt 6) / 2 := by
  obtain ⟨x, y⟩ := O
  obtain ⟨hx0, hx1, hy0, hy1⟩ := hO
  set t := minTriangleArea (eightConfig a b c d e f g h (x, y)) with htdef
  rcases (minTriangleArea_nonneg (eightConfig a b c d e f g h (x, y))).eq_or_lt with h0 | ht
  · rw [htdef, ← h0]
    nlinarith [Real.sqrt_nonneg 6, Real.sq_sqrt (show (0:ℝ) ≤ 6 by norm_num)]
  have hm : t ≤ minTriangleArea (eightConfig a b c d e f g h (x, y)) := le_rfl
  obtain ⟨b1, b2, b3, b4, b5, b6, b7, b8⟩ := budgets hA ht (hm.trans (min_le_oct _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _))
  have eEA : 0 ≤ sarea (1, e) (0, a) (x, y) := hADE 2
  have tEA := two_mul_le_sarea_of_nonneg ht eEA (area_of_le_min hm 4 0 8)
  have eHD : 0 ≤ sarea (0, h) (1, d) (x, y) := hHDE 0
  have tHD := two_mul_le_sarea_of_nonneg ht eHD (area_of_le_min hm 7 3 8)
  have eFB : 0 ≤ sarea (f, 1) (b, 0) (x, y) := hBCF 2
  have tFB := two_mul_le_sarea_of_nonneg ht eFB (area_of_le_min hm 5 1 8)
  have eCG : 0 ≤ sarea (c, 0) (g, 1) (x, y) := hBCG 1
  have tCG := two_mul_le_sarea_of_nonneg ht eCG (area_of_le_min hm 2 6 8)
  simp only [sarea] at tEA tHD tFB tCG
  obtain ⟨h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6, h7, h8, h9, h10, h11, h12⟩ := hA
  have hL : 0 < h - a := by linarith
  have hB : 0 < c - b := by linarith
  have hR : 0 < e - d := by linarith
  have hT : 0 < f - g := by linarith
  have cp1 := div_le_of_le_mul' hB b2
  have cp2 := div_le_of_le_mul' hB b3
  have cq1 := div_le_of_le_mul' hT b6
  have cq2 := div_le_of_le_mul' hT b7
  have cu1 := div_le_of_le_mul' hL b1
  have cu2 := div_le_of_le_mul' hL b8
  have cw1 := div_le_of_le_mul' hR b4
  have cw2 := div_le_of_le_mul' hR b5
  have hx0' : (0 : ℝ) ≤ 1 - x := by linarith
  have hy0' : (0 : ℝ) ≤ 1 - y := by linarith
  have := wedge_core (s := 2 * t) (X := 1 - x) (Y := y) (by linarith) hL hB hR hT (by linarith)
    (by linarith) (div_mul_self' hB) (div_mul_self' hT) (div_mul_self' hL) (div_mul_self' hR)
    (by nlinarith only [tHD, mul_nonneg (sub_nonneg.2 cp1) hx0',
      mul_nonneg (sub_nonneg.2 cp2) hx0.le])
    (by nlinarith only [tEA, mul_nonneg (by linarith : 0 ≤ 1 - h - 2 * t / (f - g)) hx0',
      mul_nonneg (by linarith : 0 ≤ 1 - e - 2 * t / (f - g)) hx0.le])
    (by nlinarith only [tFB, mul_nonneg (sub_nonneg.2 cu1) hy0',
      mul_nonneg (sub_nonneg.2 cu2) hy0.le])
    (by nlinarith only [tCG, mul_nonneg (by linarith : 0 ≤ 1 - c - 2 * t / (e - d)) hy0',
      mul_nonneg (by linarith : 0 ≤ 1 - f - 2 * t / (e - d)) hy0.le])
    (by linarith) (by linarith)
  linarith

/-! ### §6. Two neighbouring corner caps -/

/-- The largest side gap `m = max(L, B, R, T)` of the normal form, with `L = h-a`, `B = c-b`,
`R = e-d`, `T = f-g`. -/
def maxGap (a b c d e f g h : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  max (max (h - a) (c - b)) (max (e - d) (f - g))

/-- **Lemma 7** (`EIGHT_BOUNDARY:Lemma7`). For the eight boundary points of the normal form, with
`s` twice their minimum triangle area and `m = max(L, B, R, T)`, `s ≤ m(1-m)/2`. (Stated for the
eight boundary points; the proof uses only the side budgets.)
`hand/EIGHT_BOUNDARY.md`, lines 450–472.
Uses: none. -/
theorem lemma7 {a b c d e f g h : ℝ} (hA : EightAnchors a b c d e f g h) :
    2 * minTriangleArea (octagon a b c d e f g h) ≤
      maxGap a b c d e f g h * (1 - maxGap a b c d e f g h) / 2 := by
  have hLm : h - a ≤ maxGap a b c d e f g h := le_trans (le_max_left _ _) (le_max_left _ _)
  have hBm : c - b ≤ maxGap a b c d e f g h := le_trans (le_max_right _ _) (le_max_left _ _)
  have hRm : e - d ≤ maxGap a b c d e f g h := le_trans (le_max_left _ _) (le_max_right _ _)
  have hTm : f - g ≤ maxGap a b c d e f g h := le_trans (le_max_right _ _) (le_max_right _ _)
  have hcases : maxGap a b c d e f g h = h - a ∨ maxGap a b c d e f g h = c - b ∨
      maxGap a b c d e f g h = e - d ∨ maxGap a b c d e f g h = f - g := by
    simp only [maxGap]
    rcases le_total (max (h - a) (c - b)) (max (e - d) (f - g)) with hh | hh
    · rw [max_eq_right hh]
      rcases le_total (e - d) (f - g) with hh' | hh'
      · rw [max_eq_right hh']; tauto
      · rw [max_eq_left hh']; tauto
    · rw [max_eq_left hh]
      rcases le_total (h - a) (c - b) with hh' | hh'
      · rw [max_eq_right hh']; tauto
      · rw [max_eq_left hh']; tauto
  set m := maxGap a b c d e f g h
  set t := minTriangleArea (octagon a b c d e f g h) with htdef
  have hA' := hA
  obtain ⟨h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6, h7, h8, h9, h10, h11, h12⟩ := hA'
  have hm1 : m < 1 := by rcases hcases with hm | hm | hm | hm <;> rw [hm] <;> linarith
  have hm0 : 0 < m := by linarith
  rcases (minTriangleArea_nonneg (octagon a b c d e f g h)).eq_or_lt with h0 | ht
  · rw [htdef, ← h0]; nlinarith
  obtain ⟨b1, b2, b3, b4, b5, b6, b7, b8⟩ := budgets hA ht le_rfl
  have hL : 0 < h - a := by linarith
  have hB : 0 < c - b := by linarith
  have hR : 0 < e - d := by linarith
  have hT : 0 < f - g := by linarith
  have cB1 := div_le_of_le_mul' hB b2
  have cB2 := div_le_of_le_mul' hB b3
  have cT1 := div_le_of_le_mul' hT b6
  have cT2 := div_le_of_le_mul' hT b7
  have cL1 := div_le_of_le_mul' hL b1
  have cL2 := div_le_of_le_mul' hL b8
  have cR1 := div_le_of_le_mul' hR b4
  have cR2 := div_le_of_le_mul' hR b5
  have hs : 0 < 2 * t := by linarith
  rcases hcases with hm | hm | hm | hm <;> rw [hm]
  · exact gap_core hs hL hR (by linarith) hB hT (div_mul_self' hL) (div_mul_self' hR)
      (div_mul_self' hB) (div_mul_self' hT) (by linarith) (by linarith) (by linarith)
  · exact gap_core hs hB hT (by linarith) hL hR (div_mul_self' hB) (div_mul_self' hT)
      (div_mul_self' hL) (div_mul_self' hR) (by linarith) (by linarith) (by linarith)
  · exact gap_core hs hR hL (by linarith) hB hT (div_mul_self' hR) (div_mul_self' hL)
      (div_mul_self' hB) (div_mul_self' hT) (by linarith) (by linarith) (by linarith)
  · exact gap_core hs hT hB (by linarith) hL hR (div_mul_self' hT) (div_mul_self' hB)
      (div_mul_self' hL) (div_mul_self' hR) (by linarith) (by linarith) (by linarith)

/-- **Theorem 8** (`EIGHT_BOUNDARY:Theorem8`). In the normal form, if `O` lies in the central
region (11) and in both closed corner caps `conv(B,C,D,E)` and `conv(D,E,F,G)`, the minimum
triangle area is at most `21/400 < A₀`.
`hand/EIGHT_BOUNDARY.md`, lines 474–533.
Uses: EIGHT_BOUNDARY:Theorem4, EIGHT_BOUNDARY:Lemma7. -/
theorem theorem8 {a b c d e f g h : ℝ} {O : Point} (hA : EightAnchors a b c d e f g h)
    (hO : InOpenSquare O) (hc : InCentralRegion (octagon a b c d e f g h) O)
    (hBCDE : InClosedPolygon ![(b, 0), (c, 0), (1, d), (1, e)] O)
    (hDEFG : InClosedPolygon ![(1, d), (1, e), (f, 1), (g, 1)] O) :
    minTriangleArea (eightConfig a b c d e f g h O) ≤ 21 / 400 := by
  have h7 := lemma7 hA
  have hLm : h - a ≤ maxGap a b c d e f g h := le_trans (le_max_left _ _) (le_max_left _ _)
  have hRm : e - d ≤ maxGap a b c d e f g h := le_trans (le_max_left _ _) (le_max_right _ _)
  have hmo := min_le_oct a b c d e f g h O
  set m := maxGap a b c d e f g h
  obtain ⟨x, y⟩ := O
  obtain ⟨hx0, hx1, hy0, hy1⟩ := hO
  set t := minTriangleArea (eightConfig a b c d e f g h (x, y)) with htdef
  rcases (minTriangleArea_nonneg (eightConfig a b c d e f g h (x, y))).eq_or_lt with h0 | ht
  · rw [htdef, ← h0]; norm_num
  have hm : t ≤ minTriangleArea (eightConfig a b c d e f g h (x, y)) := le_rfl
  obtain ⟨b1, b2, b3, b4, b5, b6, b7, b8⟩ := budgets hA ht (hm.trans hmo)
  have eEB : 0 ≤ sarea (1, e) (b, 0) (x, y) := hBCDE 3
  have eGD : 0 ≤ sarea (g, 1) (1, d) (x, y) := hDEFG 3
  have eCF : 0 < sarea (c, 0) (f, 1) (x, y) := hc.2 1
  have tEB := two_mul_le_sarea_of_nonneg ht eEB (area_of_le_min hm 4 1 8)
  have tGD := two_mul_le_sarea_of_nonneg ht eGD (area_of_le_min hm 6 3 8)
  have tCF := two_mul_le_sarea_of_nonneg ht eCF.le (area_of_le_min hm 2 5 8)
  simp only [sarea] at tEB tGD tCF eEB eGD
  obtain ⟨h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6, h7', h8, h9, h10, h11, h12⟩ := hA
  have hL : 0 < h - a := by linarith
  have hR : 0 < e - d := by linarith
  simp only at hx0 hx1 hy0 hy1
  have hye : y ≤ e := by
    by_contra hc'; push Not at hc'
    nlinarith only [eEB, mul_pos (by linarith : (0 : ℝ) < 1 - b) (by linarith : 0 < y - e),
      mul_pos (by linarith : (0 : ℝ) < e) (by linarith : 0 < 1 - x)]
  have hyd : d ≤ y := by
    by_contra hc'; push Not at hc'
    nlinarith only [eGD, mul_pos (by linarith : (0 : ℝ) < 1 - g) (by linarith : 0 < d - y),
      mul_pos (by linarith : (0 : ℝ) < 1 - d) (by linarith : 0 < 1 - x)]
  have cu1 := div_le_of_le_mul' hL b1
  have cu2 := div_le_of_le_mul' hL b8
  have cw1 := div_le_of_le_mul' hR b4
  have cw2 := div_le_of_le_mul' hR b5
  have h18 : 1 + 2 * t / (h - a) * (e - d) + 2 * (2 * t) ≤ (1 + (e - d)) * x := by
    nlinarith only [tEB, tGD, mul_nonneg (sub_nonneg.2 cu1) (sub_nonneg.2 hye),
      mul_nonneg (sub_nonneg.2 cu2) (sub_nonneg.2 hyd)]
  have h19 : x ≤ 1 - 2 * t / (e - d) - 2 * t := by
    nlinarith only [tCF, mul_nonneg (by linarith : 0 ≤ 1 - c - 2 * t / (e - d))
      (by linarith : (0 : ℝ) ≤ 1 - y), mul_nonneg (by linarith : 0 ≤ 1 - f - 2 * t / (e - d)) hy0.le]
  have hcap := caps_core (s := 2 * t) (by linarith) hL hR hLm hRm (div_mul_self' hL)
    (div_mul_self' hR) h18 h19
  have hm0 : 0 < m := by linarith
  have hs7 : 2 * t ≤ m * (1 - m) / 2 := by linarith
  suffices hs : 2 * t ≤ 21 / 200 by linarith
  rcases le_total m (7 / 10) with hm7 | hm7
  · have hpos : 0 < m ^ 2 + 5 * m + 1 := by positivity
    have k1 : 200 * m ^ 2 ≤ 21 * (m ^ 2 + 5 * m + 1) := by
      nlinarith only [mul_nonneg hm0.le (by linarith : (0 : ℝ) ≤ 7 / 10 - m)]
    by_contra hc'
    push Not at hc'
    nlinarith only [hcap, k1, mul_lt_mul_of_pos_right hc' hpos]
  · nlinarith only [hs7, mul_nonneg (by linarith : (0 : ℝ) ≤ m - 7 / 10)
      (by linarith : (0 : ℝ) ≤ m - 3 / 10)]

/-! ### §7. A double wedge facing the opposite split -/

/-- **Theorem 9** (`EIGHT_BOUNDARY:Theorem9`). In the normal form, if `O` belongs to the closed
triangles `ADE`, `HDE`, `BFG` and `BCG`, the minimum triangle area is strictly less than
`1/20 < A₀`. (The manuscript adds: the same holds under every square symmetry; see the module
docstring. The R8 representative meets these hypotheses only after the rotation `ρ₁`, see
`EIGHT_BOUNDARY:claim-class-hypotheses`.)
`hand/EIGHT_BOUNDARY.md`, lines 537–622.
Uses: EIGHT_BOUNDARY:claim-thresholds. -/
theorem theorem9 {a b c d e f g h : ℝ} {O : Point} (hA : EightAnchors a b c d e f g h)
    (hO : InOpenSquare O)
    (hADE : InClosedPolygon ![(0, a), (1, d), (1, e)] O)
    (hHDE : InClosedPolygon ![(0, h), (1, d), (1, e)] O)
    (hBFG : InClosedPolygon ![(b, 0), (f, 1), (g, 1)] O)
    (hBCG : InClosedPolygon ![(b, 0), (c, 0), (g, 1)] O) :
    minTriangleArea (eightConfig a b c d e f g h O) < 1 / 20 := by
  obtain ⟨x, y⟩ := O
  obtain ⟨hx0, hx1, hy0, hy1⟩ := hO
  set t := minTriangleArea (eightConfig a b c d e f g h (x, y)) with htdef
  rcases (minTriangleArea_nonneg (eightConfig a b c d e f g h (x, y))).eq_or_lt with h0 | ht
  · rw [htdef, ← h0]; norm_num
  have hm : t ≤ minTriangleArea (eightConfig a b c d e f g h (x, y)) := le_rfl
  obtain ⟨b1, b2, b3, b4, b5, b6, b7, b8⟩ := budgets hA ht (hm.trans (min_le_oct _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _))
  have eEA : 0 ≤ sarea (1, e) (0, a) (x, y) := hADE 2
  have tEA := two_mul_le_sarea_of_nonneg ht eEA (area_of_le_min hm 4 0 8)
  have eHD : 0 ≤ sarea (0, h) (1, d) (x, y) := hHDE 0
  have tHD := two_mul_le_sarea_of_nonneg ht eHD (area_of_le_min hm 7 3 8)
  have eBF : 0 ≤ sarea (b, 0) (f, 1) (x, y) := hBFG 0
  have tBF := two_mul_le_sarea_of_nonneg ht eBF (area_of_le_min hm 1 5 8)
  have eGB : 0 ≤ sarea (g, 1) (b, 0) (x, y) := hBFG 2
  have tGB := two_mul_le_sarea_of_nonneg ht eGB (area_of_le_min hm 6 1 8)
  have eCG : 0 ≤ sarea (c, 0) (g, 1) (x, y) := hBCG 1
  have tCG := two_mul_le_sarea_of_nonneg ht eCG (area_of_le_min hm 2 6 8)
  simp only [sarea] at tEA tHD tBF tGB tCG
  obtain ⟨h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6, h7, h8, h9, h10, h11, h12⟩ := hA
  have hL : 0 < h - a := by linarith
  have hB : 0 < c - b := by linarith
  have hR : 0 < e - d := by linarith
  have hT : 0 < f - g := by linarith
  set s := 2 * t with hsdef
  set u := s / (h - a)
  set w := s / (e - d)
  have hu : u * (h - a) = s := div_mul_self' hL
  have hw : w * (e - d) = s := div_mul_self' hR
  have cu1 : u ≤ b := div_le_of_le_mul' hL b1
  have cu2 : u ≤ g := div_le_of_le_mul' hL b8
  have cw1 : w ≤ 1 - c := div_le_of_le_mul' hR b4
  have cw2 : w ≤ 1 - f := div_le_of_le_mul' hR b5
  -- (21), `Ty ≥ 2s`, and `x ≤ 1 - w - 3s`
  have h21 : (h - a) * (1 - x) + 2 * s ≤ (e - d) * x := by linarith only [tHD, tEA]
  have hTy : 2 * s ≤ (f - g) * y := by linarith only [tBF, tGB]
  have hx3 : x ≤ 1 - w - 3 * s := by
    nlinarith only [tCG, hTy, mul_nonneg (by linarith : 0 ≤ 1 - c - w)
      (by linarith : (0 : ℝ) ≤ 1 - y), mul_nonneg (by linarith : 0 ≤ 1 - f - w) hy0.le]
  have K1 : 0 ≤ ((e - d) + (h - a)) * (1 - w - 3 * s) - (h - a) - 2 * s := by
    nlinarith only [h21, mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left hx3 (by linarith : (0 : ℝ) ≤ (e - d) + (h - a))]
  have e1 : w * (e - d) * (e - d) = s * (e - d) := by rw [hw]
  have e2 : w * (e - d) * (h - a) = s * (h - a) := by rw [hw]
  have h22 : s * (3 * (e - d) + (h - a) + 3 * ((h - a) + (e - d)) * (e - d)) ≤
      (e - d) * (e - d) := by
    nlinarith only [mul_nonneg hR.le K1, e1, e2]
  -- (23)
  have hBK : c - b ≤ 1 - u - w := by linarith
  have hTK : f - g ≤ 1 - u - w := by linarith
  have cp := div_le_of_le_mul' hB b3
  have cq := div_le_of_le_mul' hT b6
  have hp : s / (c - b) * (c - b) = s := div_mul_self' hB
  have hq : s / (f - g) * (f - g) = s := div_mul_self' hT
  have hp0 : 0 < s / (c - b) := by positivity
  have hq0 : 0 < s / (f - g) := by positivity
  have h23 : 2 * s ≤ (1 - u - w) * (1 - (e - d)) := by
    have k1 : s ≤ s / (c - b) * (1 - u - w) := by
      nlinarith only [hp, mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left hBK hp0.le]
    have k2 : s ≤ s / (f - g) * (1 - u - w) := by
      nlinarith only [hq, mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left hTK hq0.le]
    have k3 : (e - d) + s / (c - b) + s / (f - g) ≤ 1 := by linarith
    nlinarith only [k1, k2, mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right k3 (by linarith : (0 : ℝ) ≤ 1 - u - w)]
  have := split_core (s := s) hL hR (by linarith) hu hw h22 h23
  linarith

/-! ### §8. Opposite contact intervals overlap -/

/-- **Lemma 10** (`EIGHT_BOUNDARY:Lemma10`). If two opposite side-contact intervals have disjoint
interiors (`[g,f]` and `[b,c]`, or `[a,h]` and `[d,e]`), the minimum triangle area of the eight
boundary points is at most `(3-2√2)/4 < A₀`. Consequently, at minimum area at least `A₀`,
`b < f`, `g < c`, `a < e` and `d < h`. (Stated for the eight boundary points; the proof uses only
the side budgets.)
`hand/EIGHT_BOUNDARY.md`, lines 626–660.
Uses: EIGHT_BOUNDARY:claim-thresholds. -/
theorem lemma10 {a b c d e f g h : ℝ} (hA : EightAnchors a b c d e f g h) :
    ((f ≤ b ∨ c ≤ g ∨ h ≤ d ∨ e ≤ a) →
        minTriangleArea (octagon a b c d e f g h) ≤ (3 - 2 * Real.sqrt 2) / 4) ∧
      (A₀ ≤ minTriangleArea (octagon a b c d e f g h) → b < f ∧ g < c ∧ a < e ∧ d < h) := by
  have hr2 := sqrt_two_gt
  have part1 : (f ≤ b ∨ c ≤ g ∨ h ≤ d ∨ e ≤ a) →
      minTriangleArea (octagon a b c d e f g h) ≤ (3 - 2 * Real.sqrt 2) / 4 := by
    intro hcase
    set t := minTriangleArea (octagon a b c d e f g h) with htdef
    have hr2' : Real.sqrt 2 < 3 / 2 := by
      rw [Real.sqrt_lt' (by norm_num)]; norm_num
    rcases (minTriangleArea_nonneg (octagon a b c d e f g h)).eq_or_lt with h0 | ht
    · rw [htdef, ← h0]; linarith
    obtain ⟨b1, b2, b3, b4, b5, b6, b7, b8⟩ := budgets hA ht le_rfl
    obtain ⟨h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6, h7, h8, h9, h10, h11, h12⟩ := hA
    have hL : 0 < h - a := by linarith
    have hB : 0 < c - b := by linarith
    have hR : 0 < e - d := by linarith
    have hT : 0 < f - g := by linarith
    have cB1 := div_le_of_le_mul' hB b2
    have cB2 := div_le_of_le_mul' hB b3
    have cT1 := div_le_of_le_mul' hT b6
    have cT2 := div_le_of_le_mul' hT b7
    have cL1 := div_le_of_le_mul' hL b1
    have cL2 := div_le_of_le_mul' hL b8
    have cR1 := div_le_of_le_mul' hR b4
    have cR2 := div_le_of_le_mul' hR b5
    have hs : 0 < 2 * t := by linarith
    have key : 2 * t ≤ (3 - 2 * Real.sqrt 2) / 2 := by
      rcases hcase with hc' | hc' | hc' | hc'
      · exact overlap_core hs hL hR hB hT (div_mul_self' hL) (div_mul_self' hR) (div_mul_self' hB)
          (div_mul_self' hT) (by linarith) (by linarith) (by linarith)
      · exact overlap_core hs hL hR hB hT (div_mul_self' hL) (div_mul_self' hR) (div_mul_self' hB)
          (div_mul_self' hT) (by linarith) (by linarith) (by linarith)
      · exact overlap_core hs hB hT hL hR (div_mul_self' hB) (div_mul_self' hT) (div_mul_self' hL)
          (div_mul_self' hR) (by linarith) (by linarith) (by linarith)
      · exact overlap_core hs hB hT hL hR (div_mul_self' hB) (div_mul_self' hT) (div_mul_self' hL)
          (div_mul_self' hR) (by linarith) (by linarith) (by linarith)
    linarith
  refine ⟨part1, fun hmin => ?_⟩
  have hA0 := A₀_bounds
  have hlt : (3 - 2 * Real.sqrt 2) / 4 < A₀ := by linarith
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩ <;> by_contra hc' <;> push Not at hc'
  · linarith [part1 (Or.inl hc')]
  · linarith [part1 (Or.inr (Or.inl hc'))]
  · linarith [part1 (Or.inr (Or.inr (Or.inr hc')))]
  · linarith [part1 (Or.inr (Or.inr (Or.inl hc')))]

/-! ### The octagon: convexity and nondegenerate rays -/

/-- Positive least area: no ray `O V_i` is parallel or antiparallel to another. -/
theorem raysNondegenerate_of_min_pos {a b c d e f g h : ℝ} {O : Point}
    (hpos : 0 < minTriangleArea (eightConfig a b c d e f g h O)) :
    RaysNondegenerate (octagon a b c d e f g h) O := by
  intro i j hij
  have h8i : (8 : Fin 9) ≠ i.castSucc := Fin.ne_of_val_ne (by simp; omega)
  have h8j : (8 : Fin 9) ≠ j.castSucc := Fin.ne_of_val_ne (by simp; omega)
  have := sarea_ne_zero_of_min_pos hpos 8 i.castSucc j.castSucc h8i
    (fun e => hij (Fin.castSucc_injective _ e)) h8j
  rwa [eightConfig_castSucc, eightConfig_castSucc] at this

/-- The boundary octagon of the normal form is strictly convex. -/
theorem octagon_convex {a b c d e f g h : ℝ} (hA : EightAnchors a b c d e f g h) :
    IsConvexPolygon (octagon a b c d e f g h) := by
